        intro:
            "A good morning routine can set the tone for the whole day, but most attempts at one fail within a week, not because the idea is bad but because it was built to be perfect instead of to be doable. The routines that stick are the small, low-friction, and forgiving ones, the ones you can actually follow on a bad day, not just on a motivated one. This is a practical guide to building a morning routine around what you can realistically sustain, so it becomes a habit you keep rather than a plan you abandon.",
